    {
      "bbox": [
        0.772,
        0.012,
        0.868,
        0.033
      ],
      "text": "1. Consider a relation R with five attributes ABCDE. You are given the following dependencies: A \u2192 B, BC \u2192 C, and ED \u2192 A.",
      "page_index": 2,
      "label": "text"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        0.772,
        0.033,
        0.868,
        0.055
      ],
      "text": "a) List all candidate keys for R.",
      "page_index": 2,
      "label": "text"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        0.772,
        0.053,
        0.868,
        0.075
      ],
      "text": "b) Is R in 3NF?",
      "page_index": 2,
      "label": "text"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        0.772,
        0.074,
        0.868,
        0.096
      ],
      "text": "c) Is R in BCNF?",
      "page_index": 2,
      "label": "text"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        0.772,
        0.094,
        0.868,
        0.116
      ],
      "text": "2. Suppose that we have the following three tuples in a legal instance of a relation schema S with three attributes ABC (listed in order): (1, 2, 3), (4, 2, 3), and (5, 3, 3).",
      "page_index": 2,
      "label": "text"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        0.772,
        0.11399999999999999,
        0.868,
        0.137
      ],
      "text": "a) Which of the following dependencies can you infer does not hold over schema S?",
      "page_index": 2,
      "label": "text"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        0.772,
        0.135,
        0.868,
        0.157
      ],
      "text": "b) Can you identify any dependencies that hold over S?",
      "page_index": 2,
      "label": "text"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        0.772,
        0.155,
        0.868,
        0.17700000000000002
      ],
      "text": "3. Suppose you are given a relation R with four attributes, ABCD. For the following sets of FDs: C \u2192 D, C \u2192 A, B \u2192 C, assuming those are the only dependencies that hold for R.",
      "page_index": 2,
      "label": "text"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        0.772,
        0.175,
        0.868,
        0.19799999999999998
      ],
      "text": "a) Identify the candidate key(s) for R.",
      "page_index": 2,
      "label": "text"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        0.772,
        0.196,
        0.868,
        0.218
      ],
      "text": "b) Identify the best normal form that R satisfies (1NF, 2NF, 3NF, or BCNF).",
      "page_index": 2,
      "label": "text"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        0.772,
        0.216,
        0.868,
        0.238
      ],
      "text": "\u2460 $R \\not\\exists A, B, C, D, E3$",
      "page_index": 2,
      "label": "text"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        0.772,
        0.23699999999999996,
        0.868,
        0.259
      ],
